💡 **SUGGESTION: Test gap — the "fresh rework commit + WIP commits" mix is untested**

Every squash test passes subjects that are purely WIP auto-saves, so the `sub === reworkMsg` branch of `allOurs` (line 398) — i.e. the leg that staged changes AND found timer WIP commits (`[reworkMsg, 'PROJ-123 WIP auto-save …', …]`) — is never exercised. That composite is the headline scenario in the doc line ("fold the timer's `WIP auto-save` commits **(and the rework commit)** …").

```javascript
test('fresh rework commit plus WIP auto-saves: still squashed into one', function() {
    var cmds = run(['PROJ-123 rework', 'PROJ-123 WIP auto-save a', 'PROJ-123 WIP auto-save b'], { squashReworkWip: true });
    assert.ok(has(cmds, 'git reset --soft abc1234'));
    assert.ok(has(cmds, 'git push -u --force-with-lease origin bug/PROJ-123'));
});
```

(Note the mock's staged-diff path returns empty status, so today this only exercises the subject matching — wiring a non-empty `readStagedDiffStat` would cover the full flow.)

